# Files that are executed inside Linux containers must keep LF endings.
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) a checkout would otherwise
# hand the container `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, which fails as
# "bad interpreter: no such file or directory". The docker build COPYs the
# working copy, so this is a checkout-time concern, not a commit-time one.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
docker/**/*.py  text eol=lf
